Saphira init-switch network migration RUNBOOK
============================================

Tool: saphira-net-migrate + saphira-init-switch (both in
saphira-init-switch, /usr/sbin). `apk add/del` alone migrates
nothing; the orchestrator owns the flow. Scope: network
configuration ONLY. OVS topology, identities, init packages
themselves are handled elsewhere.

The contract
------------
Changing init systems must never make remote access depend on
console recovery. lo and the management NIC come back after every
swap, or the swap does not proceed.

Identity rule
-------------
The MAC is the NIC; interface names are per-init labels
(eth0 <-> enp1s0, wlan0 <-> wlp2s0u5 are expected cases).
Every migrated stanza records its Source-MAC; systemd output
matches PermanentMACAddress=, never Name=.

systemd -> OpenRC
------------------
Deliberate path (one command):

  saphira-init-switch --to openrc [--apply-services] [--yes]

which runs: preflight migrate (dry-run; any ERROR refuses the
whole swap) -> migrate --apply (backup taken, source never
deleted) -> apk del systemd && apk add openrc (skipped if
openrc already present) -> enablement (printed always, executed
only with --apply-services) -> verify (addresses, routes,
init state).

Destination names the tool could only guess (positional
evidence, no anchoring config) stop the flow unless accepted
with --accept-heuristic-names: whatever the evidence, the files
are right before the swap or the tool refuses. There is no
post-reboot repair step.

Manual equivalent (what the orchestrator does):

1. On the RUNNING systemd machine (interface must exist for
   Name= resolution):
     saphira-net-migrate --to openrc
   Read the whole report. Every interface shows its evidence
   class (existing config, positional). Warnings list everything
   carried as comments (MTU, extra addresses/routes).
   Any ERROR aborts with zero writes: resolve it first.
2. Apply:
     saphira-net-migrate --to openrc --apply
   Destination /etc/network.d is backed up alongside itself
   (/etc/network.d.pre-migrate-<ts>). Sources are never deleted.
3. Swap init (existing del-then-add flow):
     apk del systemd && apk add openrc
4. Enablement (printed by the tool; nothing auto-enables):
     rc-update add network default
     rc-update add openvswitch default   # only if OVS present
   Ordering is existing metadata: openvswitch declares
   "before net", network provides "net".
5. Reboot. Verify: ip addr, ip route, rc-status. SSH returns.

OpenRC -> systemd
------------------
Mirror image with --to systemd. The tool emits MAC-anchored
units (/etc/systemd/network/10-<iface>.network). Enable with
systemctl enable systemd-networkd (and openvswitch if present).

OVS
---
Topology (bridges, ports, patch ports, trunks) lives in
/etc/openvswitch/conf.db, survives the swap untouched, and is
never translated. L3 on an OVS interface translates normally as
TYPE=physical with an OVS-Device provenance comment.

Rollback
--------
Both native configurations remain in place (migration never
deletes source), so reinstalling the previous init restores the
previous network path. Timestamped backups cover mistakes.
